{
  // TYPECHECK-ONLY config. an earlier Task.
  //
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: `tsconfig.json` is the BUILD config — it sets
  // `rootDir: "src"` and emits to `dist`, so it can only ever cover `src/`.
  // That meant `scripts/` and `evals/` (in this package AND at the repo root)
  // were typechecked by NOTHING: the authoritative gate's STAGE 2
  // (`the CI gate`, `cd mcp-server && npm run type-check`) read the build
  // config and therefore inherited its blind spot. Operational code that
  // mutates production data (migrations, backfills) and code that regenerates
  // gate fixtures (`scripts/regen-tool-surface-golden.ts`) sat outside every
  // check while authors believed a gate covered it.
  //
  // THE RULES ARE NOT LOOSENED. This extends the build config verbatim —
  // `strict`, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `noImplicitReturns`,
  // `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch` all still apply to the newly covered files.
  // The ONLY overrides are `noEmit` (this config never emits) and `rootDir`
  // (widened so files outside `src/` are legal members of the program at all).
  //
  // IF YOU CANNOT MAKE A FILE PASS: exclude it BY NAME below with a written
  // reason. Do NOT relax a compilerOption and do NOT exclude a directory —
  // a named exclusion is a debt someone can count and pay down; a loosened
  // option is invisible forever and removes the incentive to ever fix it.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",

  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".."
  },

  "include": [
    "src/**/*",
    // NOTE: the build config lists "tests/**/*" here, but there is NO
    // `mcp-server/tests/` directory — the 272 test files live at `src/tests/`
    // and are already covered by "src/**/*". That pattern is dead; it is not
    // repeated here, because an include that matches nothing reads as coverage.
    "scripts/**/*",
    "evals/**/*",
    "../scripts/**/*",
    "../evals/**/*"
  ],

  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",

    // ── EXCLUDED BY NAME — enumerated debt, 1 file ──────────────────────────
    //
    // ../scripts/backfill-null-embeddings.ts
    //   `import pkg from 'pg'` is UNRESOLVABLE from the repo root: the root
    //   `package.json` does not declare `pg`, and there is no `node_modules`
    //   at or above the repo root (`node -e "require.resolve('pg')"` from the
    //   repo root throws MODULE_NOT_FOUND). So this is a real runtime break,
    //   not a typecheck artifact — the script cannot run today either.
    //   Repairing it means adding a dependency to the ROOT manifest, which is
    //   outside the type-level configuration this file owns. Reported, not
    //   silently patched. Delete this line once `pg` is resolvable from the
    //   repo root; the file typechecks clean otherwise.
    "../scripts/backfill-null-embeddings.ts"
  ]
}
